    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Women of color were hit the hardest by the pandemics tool on the job market last month. The country lost 140,000 jobs in December, the first backslides since May, and all of those jobs on net belong to women. Black and Latino women have been hit the hardest with the unemployment rate among black women at 8.4% and 9.1% among Latino women. White women on the other hand have the lowest unemployment rate at 5.7%. According to government stats, women of color, especially black and Latino women, disproportionately make up industries that were hit hard by the pandemic, such as retail, restaurants, and hospitality. Those roles also often lack benefits like paid sick leave or the ability to work from home. Some experts say the widening gender gap caused by the pandemic could have an impact on the job market for years to come.",
